    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Removed:** the minor-mode count. The square with `0f0431` was the Material Design puzzle glyph (`nerd-icons-mdicon \"nf-md-puzzle\"`), missing from the font in use; the whole segment is gone (`C-h m`, or a click on the major mode box, lists the modes).\n\n**mode-line-maker** ([rougier/mode-line-maker](https://github.com/rougier/mode-line-maker), installed with `use-package :ensure (:host github ...)`): the left and right parts of the bottom line are now aligned and truncated by it.\n- Lambda: `sp-modeline-parts-compose` calls `mode-line-maker--make` (private function, the public `mode-line-maker` returns a format and lambda-line wants a string); falls back to the old `:align-to` space if the package is missing.\n- Prot: `sp-prot-modeline-format` stays one list, split at `mode-line-format-right-align` and given to `mode-line-maker`.\n- `mode-line-maker-alignment` and `-truncation-rule` apply to both; the padding face follows the theme.\n\n**Clocked task widget** (`clock` segment, right side, boxed keyword in the fourth accent colour):\n- Shows keyword, heading (cut to `sp-modeline-parts-clock-width`) and clocked time while an entry is clocked in; nothing otherwise. `mouse-1` goes to the entry, `mouse-3` opens `org-agenda`.\n- On clock-in an entry that already has an open todo keyword is switched to `sp-modeline-parts-clock-keyword` (`PROG`, in `sp-org-keywords`; `nil` to keep the state; not set if you already set `org-clock-in-switch-to-state`).\n- Fringe arrow on the clocked heading from `org-clock-in-hook` / `org-clock-out-hook`, after your snippet (`sp-modeline-parts-clock-arrow`).\n\n**Shared document:** `docs/tangles/tooling/modeline-customization.org` (differences between the lambda-line and Prot mode lines, the shared settings, recipes). The differences table was written from the code of the two modules, not from the earlier report.\n\n**Not tested** (no Emacs in the container; `.el` files only paren-checked): `mode-line-maker--make` inside lambda-line's compose, `mode-line-window-selected-p` inside its nested `format-mode-line`, the clock-in state switch with `org-clock-in-switch-to-state` as a function, the fringe arrow, and that Prot's `(mode-line-maker ...)` form works as `mode-line-format` together with the keycast anchor. Speed: the package's README says its lines draw two to three times slower.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
